WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.049 --> 00:00:04.049
With the reveal of Gear 5th, we’ve
learned the shocking truth behind Luffy’s

00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:05.230
devil fruit - for years, we’ve thought that
he ate the Gum Gum fruit, but in reality he

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.230
ate the Human Human Fruit Model: Nika - the
fruit with the most ridiculous power in the

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.230
world.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.230
Hook #2: The most ridiculous power in the
world belongs to the most ridiculous main

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.230
character in the world - but what if the weakest
members of the Straw Hats had Luffy’s God-like

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.230
abilities?

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.230
Hook #3: Today we ask the ultimate question:
Would Nami still look as good if she traded

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.230
her signature orange hair for Gear 5 Luffy’s
white locks?

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.230
With the reveal of Gear 5th, we’ve learned
the shocking truth behind Luffy’s devil

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.230
fruit - for years, we’ve thought that he
ate the Gum Gum fruit, but in reality he ate

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.490
the Human Human Fruit Model: Nika - the fruit
with the most ridiculous and insane power

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.490
in the world.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.350
And throughout the story, it kind of feels
like destiny that Luffy of all people got

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.400
to eat this fruit.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.760
In fact, it almost seems like the fruit chose
him and not the other way around.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.099
But what if the fruit had been eaten by someone
else?

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:35.380
What if instead Luffy, it was eaten by a different
Straw Hat?

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.000
And we’re not just talking about the already
strongest members of the crew like Zoro or

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.190
Sanji eating the fruit - What if the weakling
trio ate the Nika fruit?

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.860
Now, for those of you who don’t know, the
weakling trio consists of Usopp, Nami, and

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.860
Chopper.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.570
And while these three have their own strengths,
fighting is not necessarily their favorite

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.960
thing to do.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.539
In fact, these three are quicker to run away
screaming than to face down a powerful enemy.

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:08.689
But would that change if they had one of the
strongest devil fruits in all of One Piece?

00:01:08.689 --> 00:01:14.440
Usopp is probably the likeliest of the weakling
trio to actually come in contact with the

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.189
fruit.

00:01:16.189 --> 00:01:19.810
After Shanks and his crew stole the Nika fruit
from the World Government, they headed to

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.689
Foosha Village in the East Blue.

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:26.380
However, in this alternate timeline, we’re
just going to say that Yasopp the Great decided

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:33.100
to actually go visit his son instead of being
a complete deadbeat.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:38.570
All it would have taken was the Red-Hair Pirates
making a quick pit stop in Syrup Village and&nbsp;

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:42.170
Bada-Bing-Bada-Boom, we’ve got one stretchy
Usopp.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:46.700
It’s been kind of insinuated that the Nika
fruit has a will of its own.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.670
Its eluded capture by the World Government
for 800 years, after all.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:56.990
So, it very much seems like the fruit somehow
chose Luffy - but let’s just say that Usopp

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:01.770
seeing his father filled him with adventurous
spirit and courage and therefore deemed this

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:06.130
future brave warrior of the sea worthy of
its powers.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:13.390
As we know, the Hito Hito no Mi: Model Nika
appears to be just a rubber fruit before it’s

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.390
awakened.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.750
So the first result of Usopp gaining this
fruit is that he’d have a rubber body.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:24.030
One benefit of this is that his already long
nose could become even longer.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:31.410
However, the real benefit is that this power
would actually be kind of perfect for Usopp.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.239
He wouldn’t need his slingshot, Kabuto,
anymore.

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:42.950
If Usopp’s entire body was elastic, he’d
BE the slingshot.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:47.819
Just imagine how sick it would be to see Usopp
in Dressrosa making his coolest shot in the

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:53.250
series - Sugar is about to take Luffy and
Law out of commission and Usopp has to take

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.170
her out from miles away.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:03:01.629
But this time, instead of firing a round that
looks like his own face…Usopp yeets himself

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:04.610
with perfect observation haki precision.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:08.911
Beyond being able to fling projectiles (and
himself) super far, though, Usopp’s real

00:03:08.911 --> 00:03:14.170
advantage with this fruit might be the durability
that comes with being made of rubber.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:21.659
After all, few characters can take a beating
like Luffy, especially from blunt objects.

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:28.140
However, the only character that seems to
take even more damage than Luffy and then

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.360
inexplicably recover…is Usopp.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.019
Say what you will about the man - he’s not
strong.

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:37.299
He’s not always brave.

00:03:37.299 --> 00:03:41.500
But Usopp can take a hit.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:47.200
This is a guy whose whole skeleton has been
shattered on numerous occasions and then shakes

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.549
it off to be walking around in the next chapter.

00:03:49.549 --> 00:03:57.700
Now just imagine if Usopp was made of rubber:
he could probably survive beatings from Kaidou

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.110
himself.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:04.599
Would he ever be able to hit hard enough to
actually beat an opponent like that?

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:10.819
Probably not - but it would be near impossible
to knock him out.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:15.980
But would this cowardly character ever have
what it takes to become Joyboy and awaken

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.100
his devil fruit?

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:27.000
Probably not, but this video will be a whole
lot less interesting if he doesn’t, so what

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.780
would Usopp do with the powers of Sun God
Nika?

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:37.750
Usopp is a straight up inventor, consistently
making use of technologies like dials to make

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.970
weapons like Kabuto and the Clima-Tact.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.910
Having the ability to bring anything in his
imagination to life would make this creative

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.500
character super overpowered.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.900
Imagine: an overpowered Usopp.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.550
They said it couldn’t be done.

00:04:55.550 --> 00:05:02.370
All of the battles he’s won, he’s had
to do so with his ingenuity to compensate

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.169
for his lack of physical strength.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:09.250
He’s used everything from hot sauce to plants
to a paper-mache version of his own face to

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:15.050
win battles, but with the Nika fruit he could
presumably just…bring these things into

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.780
reality without much limitation.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:22.300
After all, in the Egghead Island arc, we saw
Luffy create actual physical goggles with

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:27.410
his Gear 5 powers - we’re not sure what
the upper limit is, but it seems that this

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.900
fruit can just spontaneously create objects.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:35.010
If that’s the case, then Usopp is sure to
make good use of them.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:40.660
On the other hand, it’s a bit less clear
how Nami would make use of Luffy’s devil

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:41.660
fruit.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.650
In fact, how would she find it in the first
place?

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:48.960
Well, the time that Arlong came to Nami’s
home village was around the same time that

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.870
Shanks brought the Gum Gum fruit to the East
Blue.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.660
So let’s just say that after she joined
up with the Arlong Pirates to protect her

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:00.130
village and began stealing treasure, she found
herself in Windmill Village and lifted the

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:04.389
box from the Red Hair pirates while they were
busy partying.

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:09.650
The problem is, this box didn’t contain
any gold…just a big purple piece of fruit.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:14.360
She was especially hungry that day, so voila,
rubber Nami.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.450
How would Nami use the fruit?

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:20.470
Well, in its base form when she’s just rubber,
it’s hard to say.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:24.920
One dark thought that comes to mind is that
it could actually be a disadvantage while

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.229
she was still with Arlong.

00:06:26.229 --> 00:06:30.560
The Fishmen had no reservations about making
Nami suffer, so they’d almost certainly

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.960
use the devil fruit’s weakness to water
as a method of torture…but that’s a little

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.610
morbid, so let’s get to the fun stretchy
stuff instead.

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:45.870
Nami could use her newly elastic body to squeeze
into some tight places in order to find treasure…and

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.620
then steal that treasure.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:52.670
While Luffy uses his body almost exclusively
for combat purposes, Nami would figure out

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:56.510
how to turn her new powers into a stealth
tool.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:07:01.160
She could access hard to reach places by flinging
herself into places, squeezing into tight

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.199
quarters, and so on.

00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:07.800
And if she ever was captured, it’d be no
problem for her to squeeze right out of the

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.050
bars of her jail cell.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:14.430
In addition, her mastery of the weather in
combat would gain a huge advantage.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:19.509
She already loves to summon lightning to electrocute
her opponents, but with Luffy’s rubber body,

00:07:19.509 --> 00:07:26.750
Nami could conjure as much lightning as she
wished without any risk of taking damage herself.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.490
Her thunderbolt tempo would be absolutely
insane.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.690
Talk about a shocking development.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:37.800
If Nami went Gear 5, she wouldn’t even need
the clima-tact anymore because she could just

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.860
pull lightning bolts right out the sky willy-nilly.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:49.289
If Nami managed to awaken the fruit, it would
be…well, fruitful, for her navigation career

00:07:49.289 --> 00:07:50.289
as well.

00:07:50.289 --> 00:07:55.650
The Grand Line’s seas are absolutely treacherous,
but by using Gear 5’s ability to affect

00:07:55.650 --> 00:08:00.120
terrain and make other objects bouncy, she
could just have the Thousand Sunny safely

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:05.039
trampoline its way through the New World with
little regard for the weather.

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:09.870
Depending on how exactly Nika’s imaginative
powers work, she might even be able to stop

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.889
storms or reshape the weather itself - but
we won’t know that until we get a few more

00:08:12.889 --> 00:08:13.889
answers about what exactly this fruit can
do.

00:08:13.889 --> 00:08:18.629
The truly tragic thing, though…would be
that Nami would lose the luscious orange locks

00:08:18.629 --> 00:08:21.660
she’s known for.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:27.310
And that leads us to Chopper, and we saved
the most interesting one of the bunch for

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.310
last.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:33.300
Now, Chopper has next to no reason run into
Shanks and co, so we’re going to say that

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:38.270
in this timeline, Lucky Roo got really sick
on the way back to the East Blue and the Red

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:42.460
Hair pirates had to seek medical attention
on Drum Island.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:47.610
That big piece of meat he’s always holding
must have finally gone bad and given him a

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.610
stomach bug.&nbsp;

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:52.500
For some reason their doctor, Hongo, just
couldn’t cut it this time…Also, it turns

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.839
out Shanks has a doctor on his crew: who knew?

00:08:55.839 --> 00:09:00.940
However, Dr. Kureha fixed Lucky Roo right
up, but not before a stray reindeer took a

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:06.850
bite of gum gum and turned into the walking
talking reindeer we all know and love.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:12.180
As we know, our favorite blue nosed reindeer
became super intelligent when he ate the Hito

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:18.480
Hito no Mi: Model…nothing.The plain old
human fruit gave him all the powers of a person,

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:23.240
so we’re going to imagine that the Human
Human Fruit Model Nika will still grant him

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.710
that baseline and then some.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:31.470
He’ll be the same old Chopper we’re used
to…just sillier and stretchier.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:37.900
The catch is: Chopper would awaken his fruit
waaaaaay sooner than Luffy thanks to a little

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.640
thing called the rumble ball.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.589
The rumble ball is a pill that allows Chopper
to alter his zoan fruit transformations to

00:09:45.589 --> 00:09:50.620
unlock forms that aren’t just reindeer,
human, or human-reindeer hybrid.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.880
With this he can utilize forms like brain
point, horn point, and guard point - not to

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:57.010
be confused with a point guard.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:59.590
To my knowledge Chopper has never once played
basketball.

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:03.540
Of course, Sanji got to go to a Food Wars
crossover, so maybe one day Chopper will make

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.000
his way into Slam Dunk.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.209
Hopefully not as the ball.

00:10:07.209 --> 00:10:13.280
Chopper’s transformations get insane, though,
if he overdoses on his rumble balls: if he

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:19.950
eats three rumble balls at once, things get
real crazy and he transforms into the powerful

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:20.970
Monster Point.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:26.130
A form that was incredibly cool when we first
saw it and now for some reason has the downside

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:29.680
of making him talk like an old man.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:33.250
Based on Monster Point’s similarity to the
Impel Down Jailer Beasts, who are theorized

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:38.560
to be awakened devil fruit users, this rumble
ball overdose appears to be able to force

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.160
a devil fruit to awaken.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:45.029
Another piece of evidence for this transformation
is that Bepo, Law’s mink crew mate, was

00:10:45.029 --> 00:10:50.139
able to force himself into a Sulong transformation
using a rumble ball.

00:10:50.139 --> 00:10:55.600
Mink’s sulong transformations involve the
mink growing stronger and turning white with

00:10:55.600 --> 00:11:01.339
red eyes…eerily similar to how Gear 5 Luffy
looks.

00:11:01.339 --> 00:11:05.970
The only thing is, Chopper’s monster point
and the Impel Down jailers don’t have the

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:10.130
little cloud ring that Lucci and Luffy have
in their awakened forms.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:15.839
In Japan, this is meant to resemble this thing
here called a “hagoromo” that many deities

00:11:15.839 --> 00:11:16.839
are depicted wearing.

00:11:16.839 --> 00:11:22.529
So, there’s a possibility that instead of
achieving true awakening like Luffy, Chopper’s

00:11:22.529 --> 00:11:28.800
forced awakening would be some kind of terrible,
bouncy, mindless beast - probably resembling

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:33.019
a sulong mink that can’t yet control the
power of its transformation.

00:11:33.019 --> 00:11:37.339
But assuming that the rumble ball trick does
work, Chopper would probably have awakened

00:11:37.339 --> 00:11:42.340
the Nika fruit before the rest of the crew
even arrived at Drum Island!

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:47.120
With that kind of power, this reindeer could
have kicked Wapol out of the country for sure,

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:51.089
turning Drum Island’s castle into Dr. Kureha’s
permanent residence.

00:11:51.089 --> 00:11:55.959
With Gear 5’s imagination-based powers,
he also could have brought Dr. Hiruluk’s

00:11:55.959 --> 00:11:59.650
dream to life and made Sakura trees bloom
on the island.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:05.180
Forget making the mountain look like a cherry
blossom tree, he probably just could have

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.470
gotten them to bloom for real.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:11.990
And again, we’re not sure what the limits
of this fruit are…but could Chopper use

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:16.199
it to bring his dream to life and cure any
disease?

00:12:16.199 --> 00:12:20.019
I’d like to think so, because of how this
fruit truly works, and if you want to have

00:12:20.019 --> 00:12:25.120
a complete explanation of how the Nika fruit
actually works and what its abilities really

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:28.640
can do, you can check out my video about it
right here.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.379
Shanks for watching.

